
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Setup
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

$ yolo reload
yolo: loading kernel module /lib/modules/6.8.0-117-generic/extra/yolofs.ko

$ yolo mount
yolo: mounting ~/project/.yolofs/mnt (permission=1,staging=1,prompt_timeout=30)
yolo: applying 14 rule(s) from yolofs.toml
yolo: run `yolo watch` to answer permission prompts

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Stage a change, review it, then keep or discard
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 'yolo -- <cmd>' runs <cmd> in a staging overlay and prints what it changed.

$ yolo -- sh -c 'echo "hello, yolofs" > greeting.txt'
greeting.txt (added)
yolo: snapshot [1] · 1 staged change · yolo travel 1 to return
# 'review' summarizes the staged changes; '--diff' shows the content.

$ yolo review
greeting.txt (added)

1 staged change
(latest snapshot · more: `yolo review [<id>|a..b|all] [--diff] [--each]`)

$ yolo review --diff
greeting.txt (added)
+hello, yolofs
(latest snapshot · more: `yolo review [<id>|a..b|all] [--diff] [--each]`)
# 'commit' writes staging out to the real files.

$ yolo commit
Committed 1 change.

$ cat greeting.txt
hello, yolofs
# 'abort' throws staging away instead — the real directory is never touched.

$ yolo -- sh -c 'echo oops > mistake.txt'
mistake.txt (added)
yolo: snapshot [1] · 1 staged change · yolo travel 1 to return

$ yolo abort --force
Staging discarded.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Snapshots, history & travel
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every run auto-snapshots, so you can review across them and rewind.

$ yolo -- sh -c 'echo step1 > step1.txt'
step1.txt (added)
yolo: snapshot [1] · 1 staged change · yolo travel 1 to return

$ yolo -- sh -c 'echo step2 > step2.txt'
step2.txt (added)
yolo: snapshot [2] · 1 staged change · yolo travel 2 to return
# 'review all' is everything vs base; '--each' breaks it out per snapshot.

$ yolo review all
step2.txt (added)
step1.txt (added)

2 staged changes

$ yolo review --each
snapshot [1]
step1.txt (added)

snapshot [2]
step2.txt (added)
# 'travel' rewinds the working tree to a snapshot — step2 disappears.

$ yolo travel 1
Traveled to snapshot "after sh -c echo step1 > step1.txt" (1 staged change).

$ yolo -- sh -c 'ls step*.txt'
step1.txt
(no changes)
# 'timeline' is the snapshot graph; after travel the abandoned branch is dimmed.

$ yolo timeline
  snapshot [1] after sh -c echo step1 > step1.txt
  snapshot [2] after sh -c echo step2 > step2.txt (unreachable)
  travel    [3] traveled to [1] (unreachable)

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Permission rules & the 'yolo watch' daemon
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 'deny' blocks a path; the attempt is logged as an access note.

$ yolo rule deny secret.txt
rule set: secret.txt = deny (live)

$ yolo -- sh -c 'cat secret.txt'
cat: secret.txt: Permission denied
yolo: command exited with 1

Observed accesses (not staged):
  blocked  read  secret.txt
# 'ask' defers to the 'yolo watch' daemon (no daemon => denied). Interactively
# it prompts [a]llow/[r]ead/[h]ide/[d]eny; here it runs --allow-all in the background.

$ yolo rule ask apikey.txt
rule set: apikey.txt = ask (live)

$ yolo watch --allow-all &
yolo: watching for permission requests — allowing all (Ctrl-C to stop)

$ yolo -- sh -c 'cat apikey.txt'
[ask] read ~/project/apikey.txt (pid=48213 cat)
  → allow (req #2)
token

Observed accesses (not staged):
  blocked  read  secret.txt
  ask      read  apikey.txt → allow

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Teardown
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

$ yolo abort --force
Staging discarded.

$ yolo unmount
yolo: unmounted ~/project/.yolofs/mnt

$ yolo unload
yolo: unloading kernel module
